rix $C$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{22}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302334 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0bc11750-a747-519f-92bc-e4276b877d58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302334 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $C$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -6 & -7 \\\\ \\,\\,0\\,\\, & -\\frac{1}{2} & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${u}_{22}=-6,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{22}=(-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (-6)=3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302335 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301288 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302335 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32749" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302335 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302335 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $D=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $D$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{23}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302335 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "27eaf5c2-ea09-500f-97aa-b8eb299f8da3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302335 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $D$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ -1 & \\,\\frac{1}{3}\\, & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${u}_{23}=9,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{23}=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9=3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402061 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402061 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402063 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402061 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402061 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402061 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402061 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402061 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402061 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186402065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402061 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a81fb830-b280-555b-983a-34f12dd2e101" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402062 #edb/ref 1080 "0,\\,-2,\\,3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402062 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402062 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "24743710-ccae-5ce6-b9bd-ec3e3a56e15a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402063 #edb/ref 1080 "0,\\,-5,\\,3" #edb/